# KNOWN GAP — the WORST cell of the opaque-handle receiver-ABI class: no `&`
# sigil anywhere, `gg check` clean, no crash, and it prints a heap pointer as
# an integer. A user would never suspect it.
#
#   gg check : exit 0
#   gg build : exit 0
#   run      : prints `187650740445858`, exit 0
#
# INTENDED: `2`, exit 0.
#
# ROOT CAUSE — a RECEIVER-ABI mismatch, shared with the `&`-param cell (see
# known_gaps/mutex_amp_param_lost_writes_and_segv.gg). An opaque handle type IS
# a pointer (`typedef GorgetAtomicInt* AtomicInt`), and these 12 protocols take
# self BY VALUE (`SelfConvention::ByValue`): Shared · Weak · Mutex · RWLock ·
# Thread · AtomicInt · AtomicBool · Barrier · WaitGroup · Semaphore · OnceFlag ·
# TaskGroup. Any route that hands such a callee a POINTER-typed receiver passes
# one indirection too many, and the callee reinterprets whatever it points at as
# the handle struct. Types with Borrow/MutBorrow self (Vector, Dict, String,
# Guard…) are correct — `Guard[int] &g` prints 42.
#
# ⚠ THE `&` SIGIL IS NOT THE DISCRIMINATOR. Measured 2026-08-05, three routes,
# only one of which uses a sigil:
#   struct field    b.c.add(1)          -> prints garbage, exit 0  (THIS FILE)
#   collection elem v[0].add(1)         -> SEGV 139
#   `&` param       bump(&c)            -> silently prints 0
# and the BARE param is CORRECT (prints 2), because these types have INTERIOR
# MUTABILITY -- mutation through the handle needs no `&` at all.
#
# CONSEQUENCE FOR THE FIX (owner-decided 2026-08-05): rejecting `&` on opaque
# handles would fix ZERO of the two sigil-free routes, so it is not a smaller
# version of the fix -- it is a spec carve-out that leaves the class live.
# `docs/language-reference.md:605-613` also makes `Type &name` universal with no
# exception. The fix is to LOWER CORRECTLY: reconcile receiver-vs-ABI at one
# chokepoint, emitting the missing dereference when a ByValue callee is handed a
# pointer receiver.
#
# Graduate out of known_gaps/ (un-ignore + move) the round this is fixed, and
# graduate the sibling `&`-param and collection-element cells with it -- one
# root, three routes, one axis-complete net.

from std.sync import AtomicInt

struct Bag:
    AtomicInt c

void main():
    Bag b = Bag(AtomicInt(0))
    b.c.add(1)
    b.c.add(1)
    print(b.c.load())
